Third-party forcing data — provenance and attribution
======================================================

The per-case subdirectories here (BOMEX/, RICO/, DYCOMS_RF01/, DYCOMS_RF02/,
ARM9707/, ASTEX209/, TOGA/, LBA/, GATE_IDEAL/) contain SAM/gSAM CASE decks
(ASCII `grd`, `lsf`, `prm`, `snd`, `sfc`, `rad` files) used to drive the legoESM
LES/CRM idealized cases.

Source
------
These decks originate from the System for Atmospheric Modeling (SAM) / gSAM,
authored by Marat Khairoutdinov (Stony Brook University).
  - SAM: http://rossby.msrc.sunysb.edu/~marat/SAM.html
  - Reference: Khairoutdinov, M. F., and D. A. Randall (2003), "Cloud Resolving
    Modeling of the ARM Summer 1997 IOP: Model Formulation, Results,
    Uncertainties, and Sensitivities", J. Atmos. Sci., 60, 607-625.

They are redistributed here (unmodified idealized-case input decks) for
reproducibility of the legoESM smoke/validation cases. Credit for the case
setups belongs to the SAM/gSAM authors and the respective field-campaign
communities (BOMEX, RICO, DYCOMS-II, ARM, GATE, LBA, etc.).

Regenerating / refreshing
-------------------------
`scripts/data/fetch_les_forcing.py` repopulates this cache from any gSAM
checkout (point it at the checkout root via `--gsam-root` or `$LEGOESM_GSAM_ROOT`).
`legoesm.atmosphere.forcing.sam_case_forcing.resolve_sam_case_dir` falls back to
this cache, so once populated the gSAM-backed drivers find their decks with no
external checkout.
